                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Correct. A lead acid battery is a secondary battery that produces a high current. The battery is dead when the reaction quotient, "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "Q"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", equals the equilibrium constant, "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ". A primary battery cannot be recharged and secondary batteries are rechargeable."
