              "legacyMatch": "D,E",
              "rule": "(!(input like {B})) && ((!(input like {A})) && (input like {D} && (input like {C} && (input like {E}))))",
              "score": 5
            },
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. The voltage of a battery is the same as the cell potential of the battery, which is based on the half-reactions and the substances involved in the half-reactions. Doubling the size of the battery does not change the half-reactions or the substances, and the cell potential does not change."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "a3c0a29729ce4c61976ffd1d4c699066",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A battery is simply a galvanic cell that is specifically built to be a power source, and therefore, the principles for a galvanic cell still apply to a battery. It is useful to consider the version of the Nernst equation that relates equilibrium and the equilibrium constant to changes to the cell potential as the battery is used: "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "fab5363351954044bd51e807294fcadf",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "E_{cell}\\;=\\;{E^\\circ}_{cell}\\;-\\;\\frac{RT}{nF}\\ln\\;Q",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "df186d8d8bce4ac28db950ddbc6f76d8",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "It is also useful to consider the relationship between the standard cell potential and the equilibrium constant:"
                      }
